# RetroReportOverdue, lifted VERBATIM out of prometheusrule.yaml (comments stripped — the
# manifest is its one home) — the rules file that retro-report.promtool-test loads. Not a
# manifest and not applied to anything: `promtool test rules` needs upstream-format rules
# (top-level `groups:`), and a PrometheusRule keeps them under `.spec`, so the CR cannot be
# loaded directly. Named .promtool-rules rather than .yaml on purpose — manifest-lint
# kubeconforms EVERY *.yaml under argocd/resources and a non-manifest there would fail it.
#
# ONE ALERT, its OWN file (homelab#591, 2026-08-19): RetroReportOverdue used to be one of the
# five alerts hand-copied into agent-runs.promtool-rules. The restart-gap harden below is a
# DIFFERENCE-shaped contract — "the alert must survive a pushgateway wipe of a <8d-old success,
# and must still fire on a genuinely >8d-stale one" — which is exactly the kind of thing that
# needs its own dedicated behaviour fixture rather than sharing a file with four unrelated
# alerts (the AgentCoordinateScanWedged precedent in agent-runs.promtool-rules' own header:
# "duplicating it here would give it two homes and one of them would rot"). Moved out, not
# duplicated — agent-runs.promtool-rules/-test no longer mention RetroReportOverdue at all.
#
# ⚠ THIS COPY IS NOT DRIFT-PINNED beyond `devbox run prometheus-rules-lint`'s bidirectional CR↔copy
# pin (homelab#337/#375, see that script) — re-copy after editing the alert.
#
#   yq -o=json '{"groups": [{"name": "agent-runs", "rules": [.spec.groups[].rules[] | select(.alert == "RetroReportOverdue")]}]}' argocd/resources/pushgateway/prometheusrule.yaml | yq -P '.'
#
# ONE LINE on purpose — yq 4.x's lexer rejects a newline inside the expression ("lexer: invalid
# input text"); the group name stays "agent-runs" because that is the CR's group the alert lives
# in (`.spec.groups[].rules[]` is `select()`-filtered by alert name only, not moved to a new
# group). Verified by RUNNING the line above on 2026-08-19: its output is byte-identical to the
# body below.
groups:
  - name: agent-runs
    rules:
      - alert: RetroReportOverdue
        expr: (time() - (max(max_over_time(retro_report_last_success_timestamp[8d])) or vector(0))) > 8 * 86400
        for: 6h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          platform_machinery: "true"
        annotations:
          summary: No retro report has landed in >8 days — ADR-103 weekly KPI scoring is not producing data
          description: 'The Monday 05:00Z retro-session CronWorkflow (the platform series, stack=platform since homelab#588) has not landed a report PR in over 8 days (or has never landed one since the belt shipped 2026-08-10). This can mean the cron is firing and guard-refusing, OR that a genuinely recent success just cannot be SEEN — as of homelab#591 the expr bridges a pushgateway wipe via Prometheus''s own 8d retention, so if this fires the last landed report really is stale. Check the newest retro-session workflow in ns agent-coordinator and re-fire via: argo -n agent-coordinator submit --from cronworkflow/retro-session. KPI spec: docs/agents/retros/BRIEF.md; belt design: FU-058.'
